from c8e_base import *
LB(8,5,'Language work: antonyms, word substitution, suffixes, acronyms, clipping, passive voice and a report','Language work for Bibha Chowdhuri: antonyms, suffixes -ship -ment -hood, acronyms, clipping and the passive voice','Words that honour a woman scientist',
 "Bibha Chowdhuri was a pioneer of Indian science, and a star was renamed Bibha in her honour. The language work of her lesson teaches us opposites, exact words, suffixes, acronyms, clipping, the passive voice and report writing.",
 [("Antonyms are words with opposite meanings. The antonym of dependent is independent, of weakness is strength, of trivial is important or significant, and of neglect is care. Use the text to check the other crossword clues.","dependent/independent, weakness/strength"),
  ("Six exact words replace long phrases. Pioneers are the first people to start something, a physicist studies matter, energy and light, peers are people of your own age or group, luminaries are famous and important people, persistence is continuous effort and determination, and barriers are things that block your way.","pioneers, physicist, peers, luminaries, persistence, barriers"),
  ("The suffix -ship forms words such as membership, partnership, citizenship, professorship and leadership. It shows a state, position or relationship.","-ship"),
  ("The suffix -ment forms government, entertainment, agreement and achievement from the verbs govern, entertain, agree and achieve. It makes a noun from a verb.","-ment"),
  ("The suffix -hood forms childhood and brotherhood. It shows a stage of life or a bond.","-hood"),
  ("An acronym is an abbreviation read as a word. In the grid, NASA stands for National Aeronautics and Space Administration, AIIMS for All India Institute of Medical Sciences, AYUSH for Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homoeopathy, NIPER for National Institute of Pharmaceutical Education and Research, and WHO for World Health Organization. ISRO and STEM are acronyms too.","acronyms"),
  ("Clipping makes a shorter word from a longer one. Back clipping keeps the front: exam from examination, ad from advertisement, memo from memorandum, gym from gymnasium, photo from photograph and lab from laboratory.","back clipping"),
  ("Front clipping keeps the end: phone from telephone, net from internet and bike from motorbike. Middle clipping keeps the middle: flu from influenza and fridge from refrigerator.","front and middle clipping"),
  ("In the active voice the subject performs the action, as in 'Scientists discovered a cure'. In the passive voice the subject receives the action, as in 'A cure was discovered'. The passive is made with a form of be plus the past participle.","active and passive voice"),
  ("Use the passive when the action matters more than the doer, as in 'A cure for the disease was discovered', when the doer is obvious, as in 'The national anthem is sung at the start of the event', or when the doer is unknown, as in 'The car was stolen last night'.","when to use the passive"),
  ("In the news report on the malaria vaccine, the verbs become were recorded, was discovered, was tested, were published, were taken and was measured, because the verb must agree with its subject.","passive in a report"),
  ("To rewrite the plant experiment, begin 'An experiment was conducted to investigate the effects of light on plant growth', and carry on with 'Various plants were placed...', 'Their growth was measured...' and 'Data was recorded daily'.","rewriting in the passive"),
  ("The Chandrayaan landing steps are a process, so use the present passive: the spacecraft is launched, it is positioned, its path is adjusted, it is slowed down and the rover is released.","process in the passive"),
  ("For the report on the Zonal Science Exhibition, use the past tense, the passive voice and the third person, with a headline, the reporter's name and three paragraphs covering who, when, where, why, the competitions and the winners.","report writing"),
  ("In the listening task you hear a podcast on Artificial Intelligence and choose answers on healthcare, the pandemic, renewable energy, education and accessibility. For speaking, hold a panel discussion on mobile phones with a moderator, principal, teacher, parent and student.","listening and speaking")],
 ("Add a suffix to 'citizen' and rewrite 'Scientists measured the plants' in the passive voice.",
  [("Citizen plus -ship gives citizenship.","-ship shows a state or position."),
   ("The plants were measured by scientists.","Use were plus the past participle, and keep the doer with by if needed.")]),
 ("Explain when we use the passive voice, with an example.",
  ["the passive is used when the action matters more than the doer","also when the doer is obvious or unknown","a correct passive example such as The car was stolen last night"],
  ["Using the passive for every sentence","Forgetting the past participle after was or were"]),
 ["Antonyms: dependent/independent, weakness/strength.","Suffixes: -ship, -ment, -hood.","Acronyms are read as words: NASA, AIIMS, AYUSH, NIPER, WHO.","Clipping: back (exam), front (phone), middle (flu).","Passive voice: be plus past participle, used when the action matters more than the doer."],
 [mcq("v5c-1",1,"The antonym of 'dependent' is","independent",[("dependable","Dependable means reliable."),("depending","This is a verb form.")],"Dependent and independent are opposites."),
  mcq("v5c-2",1,"'Famous and important people' is one word:","luminaries",[("peers","Peers are people of the same age or group."),("barriers","Barriers block the way.")],"Luminaries."),
  mcq("v5c-3",1,"Which word means 'a scientist who studies matter, energy and light'?","physicist",[("pioneer","A pioneer is a first starter."),("mentor","A mentor is a guide.")],"A physicist."),
  mcq("v5c-4",1,"Adding -hood to 'child' makes","childhood",[("childship","This is not a word."),("childment","This is not a word.")],"Childhood."),
  mcq("v5c-5",1,"Which is an acronym?","NASA",[("TV","This is read letter by letter."),("km","This is a short form, not read as a word.")],"NASA is read as a word."),
  mcq("v5c-6",2,"Adding -ment to 'govern' makes","government",[("governship","This is not a word."),("governhood","This is not a word.")],"Government."),
  mcq("v5c-7",2,"'Flu' from 'influenza' is an example of","middle clipping",[("back clipping","Back clipping keeps the front part."),("front clipping","Front clipping keeps the end part.")],"Flu keeps the middle."),
  mcq("v5c-8",2,"'Phone' from 'telephone' is an example of","front clipping",[("back clipping","Back clipping keeps the front part."),("middle clipping","Middle clipping keeps the middle.")],"Phone keeps the end."),
  mcq("v5c-9",2,"Which sentence is in the passive voice?","The car was stolen last night.",[("Thieves stole the car.","This is active."),("The thief is running.","This is active.")],"Was stolen is the passive."),
  mcq("v5c-10",2,"'A new vaccine for malaria ___ in the lab.' Choose the correct passive form.","was discovered",[("discovered","This is the active past tense."),("were discovered","The subject is singular.")],"Was discovered."),
  mcq("v5c-11",3,"Why is the passive used in 'The national anthem is sung at the start of the event'?","The doer is obvious.",[("The doer is unknown.","We know people sing it."),("The sentence is a question.","It is a statement.")],"We do not need to say who sings it."),
  mcq("v5c-12",3,"'The spacecraft ___ towards the Moon.' Choose the present passive.","is launched",[("was launched","This is past, but the steps are written in the present."),("launches","This is active.")],"The steps are a process, so use the present passive.")])
